  <title>Catalog creator</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Catalog creator</gui></guiseq> picks the
  products for your catalog, gives each a picture, and fills in the catalog
  template in LibreOffice. The products chosen and their order are kept, so
  the catalog can be updated and printed again later.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Customer markup percent</gui> whose prices the
    catalog shows, and the <gui>Image size for view</gui>. Check <gui>Load
    description</gui> to show each product's description. Click <gui>Load
    catalog</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Add products by choosing them in the box above the list. They
    are added to the catalog at once.</p></item>
    <item><p>Select a product and click <gui>Update image</gui> to choose its
    picture.</p></item>
    <item><p>Drag products up and down the list to set the order they
    print in.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Populate template</gui> to open the finished catalog
    in LibreOffice.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p><gui>Remove product</gui> takes the selected product out of the catalog.
  Right click a product for its <gui>Product hub</gui> or <gui>Preview
  image</gui>, which shows its picture full size in a window of its own.</p>

</page>
